# Environments

One repo. Two deploy environments. Secrets live only in each platform's secret store, never in a committed `.env`.

| Layer | Staging | Production |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Git branch | `staging` | `production` |
| Supabase | `tunetalez-staging` | production project (own ref) |
| Cloudflare Pages | `tunetalez-web-staging` → `staging.tunetalez.com` | `tunetalez-web` → apex/www |
| R2 | `tunetalez-media-staging` → `media-staging.tunetalez.com` | `tunetalez-media-prod` → `media.tunetalez.com` |
| EAS | `preview` profile (later) | `production` profile (later) |
| Secrets | GitHub Environment `staging` | GitHub Environment `production` + required reviewer |
| Local | `.env.local` (gitignored) → staging only | — |

# CI rules

- Use `node-version-file: .nvmrc` and `npm ci` (commit `package-lock.json`).
- Before `supabase db push`, run `supabase link --project-ref $SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF` with `SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD` set (non-interactive).
- Staging CI pushes schema only — **never** `--include-seed`.
- Never hardcode a production credential.
- Never let a non-production branch touch the production Supabase project.
- Push to `staging` deploys staging. Only a reviewed merge into `production` deploys live.
- Local machines talk only to staging.
